  "construction": [
    "The Taylor integral samples (t*0,theta)=(0,theta); its actual factor root jets cost one numerator derivative and the planar 2^n norm comparison.",
    "The existing actual factor extension is only used as a smooth germ. All numerator and factor ordinary root jets are transferred by equality on the genuine open strip.",
    "The physical mixed-jet variant uses both root orientations through the single signed-shift theorem; only the same physical turning-circle point appears on the right-hand side.",
    "Every stated bound holds for any positive qualitative strip radius satisfying the actual strip conditions, with no radius or derivative of its clamp on the right-hand side."
  ],
  "limits": [
